# THE GAZE (Shoulder.GAZE_LEAST, 19_colossi `gaze`): over the shoulder, turned
# toward the looming colossus, the mouse tips the view far enough up to take the
# whole machine in -- its hub stands 45 degrees up -- where the ordinary limit
# shows two legs leaving the top of the frame. Turned away from it, the view
# eases back down on its own; frames a third of a second apart show it coming
# home without a jump.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_gaze.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=12 --view=shoulder --weather=clear:0
wait 3
shot 00-level with land:coast
mouse 830,0 1
wait 1
shot 01-turned-toward-it with land:coast
mouse 0,-2400 1.5
wait 0.5
shot 02-looking-up-at-it with land:coast
mouse -830,0 1
shot 03-turned-away with land:coast
wait 0.33
shot 04-coming-home with land:coast
wait 0.33
shot 05-coming-home with land:coast
wait 0.33
shot 06-coming-home with land:coast
wait 2
shot 07-home with land:coast
